  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I worked all 13 members of 'Okafor CRC 2026' under RBC-QM-02. 8 had an open gap. For each of them I ordered a mailed FIT kit (LAB-FIT-KIT, routine, window 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31) and sent a portal message saying the kit is on its way and how to complete and return it. None of them already had an active FIT order. I placed no orders and sent no messages for the other 5, and wrote nothing about anyone outside the group.\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (72) | Excluded | Age 66 or older, active frailty diagnosis (since 2025-09), and on donepezil, a dementia medication, active since 2025-06 and still listed in the Jan 2026 note. |\n| pt-0011 Marilu Gaona (62) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0001, message comm-t0009 | No qualifying screening on record. Her hospice episode ended 2025-10-20, before 2026, so it does not exclude her. |\n| pt-0014 Santo Pagac (55) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0002, message comm-t0010 | A colonoscopy was ordered (sr-00002), but he did not show for the 2026-04-14 appointment. An order or appointment is not screening. |\n| pt-0018 Lance Muller (53) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0003, message comm-t0011 | His stool DNA-FIT sample was collected 2023-12-27, before the 2024–2026 lookback; it counts by collection date, not the 2024-01 result date. His 2021 FIT is too old. |\n| pt-0019 Harrison O'Keefe (68) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0004, message comm-t0012 | Has active frailty, but no advanced illness. His donepezil was stopped 2023-03-20 (testing showed mild cognitive impairment, not dementia), so no dementia medication in 2025–2026. Lives at home. No screening. |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (52) | Excluded | Hospice episode 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21 (finished), which falls in the measurement period. |\n| pt-0021 Ángela Vigil (52) | Excluded | Total proctocolectomy in 2015, from a scanned outside operative report (doc-00059). |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (51) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0005, message comm-t0013 | Her last FIT sample was collected 2025-12-29 (resulted 2026-01-05), so it falls outside 2026. No other screening. |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (51) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0006, message comm-t0014 | Her 2024-06 stool blood test is outside 2026, and the 2025 colonoscopy order was never completed. |\n| pt-0034 Rickey Sipes (72) | Excluded | Age 66 or older and lives long term at Maple Grove Care Center (home address Room 214, nursing facility visits Feb and Jul 2026). |\n| pt-0035 Elvin Wolff (68) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0007, message comm-t0015 | His May 2026 nursing facility stay was short-term rehab after hip surgery, and he went home. No frailty or advanced illness, no screening. |\n| pt-0036 Nick Bartoletti (53) | Open gap: FIT sr-t0008, message comm-t0016 | His 2021 sigmoid colectomy removed only part of the colon, which does not exclude. No screening. |\n| pt-0037 Fumiko Pouros (35) | Not in population | Born 1991-02-04, so 35 at the end of 2026, below the 46–75 range. |\n\nTwo active colonoscopy orders remain open that I did not touch: sr-00002 (pt-0014) and sr-00003 (pt-0024, whose window ended 2025-06-30). You may want to close or follow up on them.",
